# ADR-000: Bootstrap

## Status

Accepted on bootstrap.

## Context

`{{ project_name }}` was created from the `service-dotnet` Copier template at `ika100/sdlc-foundry`. The template encodes the platform's .NET service conventions (platform ADR-127):

- .NET {{ dotnet_major }} LTS SDK via devbox; C# with nullable reference types, central package versions and lock files
- ASP.NET Core minimal APIs on Kestrel, JSON log lines on stdout{% if needs_observability %}, prometheus-net metrics on `/metrics`, OpenTelemetry tracing (OTLP when `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` is set){% endif %}
{%- if needs_database %}
- PostgreSQL through EF Core and Npgsql; migrations in `src/{{ namespace }}/Data/Migrations/` (dotnet-ef), applied at startup; Testcontainers tests
{%- endif %}
- `dotnet format` + the .NET analyzers (warnings are errors) as the quality gate; trivy for the locked packages
- xUnit with an 80 % line coverage gate (coverlet); smoke tests of category `smoke`
- Chiseled .NET image, numeric non-root user → `{{ docker_registry }}/{{ project_name }}`
- No Kubernetes manifests here: the system's gitops-app repo owns them (platform ADR-017); this repo ships a container image
- GitHub topic `deployable-service` for ArgoCD discovery
- Claude Code agents from the `sdlc-foundry` marketplace (`svc-dotnet` + `svc` + `shared`)

## Decision

We adopt the platform conventions verbatim. Any deviation must be justified in a new ADR.

## Consequences

Skeleton updates (CI, devbox recipes, Dockerfile, .NET bump, build and analyzer settings) arrive through `copier update`; `src/`, `tests/`, `Directory.Packages.props`, the solution and `docs/adr/` are project-owned and never overwritten.
